 "about_text": "Currency Exchange (CXLA) is a Los Angeles gallery and community arts space that pairs its exhibition schedule with social-practice programming. Rather than functioning as a conventional white-box gallery, it uses its ground-floor space—situated within affordable housing along the West Washington corridor in Mid-City—as a gathering point for artists, residents, and neighbors. Alongside rotating exhibitions, CXLA runs Community Feeds tied to each show's closing, karaoke nights during exhibitions, artist talks, workshops, and a Beauty Salon series developed with Transformation Arts and the Agape Artist Residency. It also produces a neighborhood zine documenting Mid-City businesses and stories, and invites residents to create collaborative lobby artworks. The organization frames its programming as an investment in the surrounding community's social fabric.",
